<!--
  Editor colour scheme for the Synthwave '85 theme. The palette of
  ghostty/config, zsh/colors.zsh, chrome/theme and vscode/theme, with the same
  roles: cyan is what you call, gold is text you wrote, coral is control flow
  and anything wrong, magenta is structure, #495495 is what you skim past.

  parent_scheme="Darcula" matters: anything not named here inherits from
  Darcula rather than falling back to the light defaults, so a language this
  file never heard of still looks right.

  Colours have no leading # in this format. The CONSOLE_*_OUTPUT block at the
  bottom is the Ghostty palette verbatim, so the IDE's terminal and run output
  are the terminal.
-->
